big dave says:

 >while eating is a required periodic necessity in the dungeon its
 >most useful purpose is to gain intrinsics.  it should then have

Very seldom do you eat to get intrinsics.  The ratio is 10-1, if not
higher, until it the ratio gets even worse as your character already
has most of the intrinsics.  In my original post I agreed that one
could choke while trying to gain something, I once did that when 
I was at the Castle level and didn't have fire resistance.  When
the character died I had no complaint.  But when there character
knows that there is nothing to gain it makes *NO* sense that he 
would choke to death.  Do you postulate that they have no control
over themselves once they begin to eat?  Or are you saying that 
they are so stupid that they ignore the discomfort?  Anyone that
stupid would trip and fall on their sword.  If the character has
no control than *whenever* you eat it should say "Ajax uncontrolable
gorges himself with almost no regard for his life".  No character
should be able to choke without the "do you want to continue?"
message.  It makes *no* sense and does not belong in the game unless
the messages change.  I've had characters die without no warning
eating and also drinking potions.


 >1) the game has to tell you that you're full.

It does not.  "Sated" to me means not hungry at all, not full to the
point of vomiting and choking on it.  And how often does anyone do
that anyway?  The Romans has Vomitoriums, I doubt they'd do that if
they collected dead bodies.

 >2) the game has to give you a clue that you're having a hard time eating.

It does not always.  

 >3) the game has to give you an indication when it is safe to eat.

Maybe the message needs to be spit out into "sated" and "gorged".

 >4) the game has to provide some means for you to preserve food.

Not needed.  I only use the tinning kit if it's cursed.

 >without these then choking is unreasonable!!!  what? the game already
